<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 pct.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose an adjusted 6.0 percent in the week to May 14 over the equivalent year-ago week, data released by the Bank of England showed. Last week the annual rise was 6.4 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     21.24	  21.63	   20.04</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.16	  2.20	     1.92</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
